# Line endings for this repository.
#
# Git already stores every text file here with LF. What it did NOT do was say
# how to check one out, so a clone on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` wrote
# CRLF into the working tree — and the brand gate compares a committed SVG
# byte for byte against what its generator writes, which is LF. All 48 social
# assets failed on Windows and passed in CI, which is the worst shape a gate
# can have: red for whoever is working, green for whoever is reviewing.
#
# `eol=lf` is what fixes it, and it beats `core.autocrlf` rather than asking
# every person to configure it. Any file a generator writes and a test reads
# back has to come out of git exactly as the generator would write it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never looks at the bytes. PNGs are the reason this list
# exists: 61 of them contain a CR+LF pair by coincidence, and `text=auto`
# classifies them by their NUL bytes rather than by that pair. Saying it here
# does not change today's behaviour — it makes the next image format somebody
# commits safe without anybody having to know the heuristic.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# SVG is text, and deliberately not in the list above: it is generated,
# compared and diffed as text, and it must be LF.
